content='`docker build` only looks for a file called **Dockerfile** (capital “D”) in the\ndirectory you give it as the build context.  \nIn your repository the file is inside `src/`, so when you run\n\n```bash\ndocker build .\n```\n\nDocker cannot find a Dockerfile in the current directory.  \nIt therefore tries to treat the string “dockerfile” as an image name and you get\n\n```\ninvalid reference format: "FROM ubuntu"\n```\n\nand later\n\n```\nno such file or directory: dockerfile\n```\n\n### What you need to do\n\n1. **Place the Dockerfile in the build‑context directory**  \n   Either move it to the root of the repository (or wherever you run the\n   command) or specify its location with `-f`.\n\n2. **Make sure the file is named exactly `Dockerfile`**  \n   On Linux the name is case‑sensitive; `dockerfile` or `Dockerfile.txt` will\n   not be recognized.\n\n3. **Run the build from the directory that contains the Dockerfile**  \n   ```bash\n   # if Dockerfile is in the repo root\n   cd myrepo\n   docker build -t myapp .\n   ```\n\n   or, if you keep it in `src/`:\n\n   ```bash\n   docker build -f src/Dockerfile -t myapp .\n   ```\n\n### Example Dockerfile\n\n```dockerfile\n# Dockerfile\nFROM ubuntu:22.04\n\n# Install Python and pip\nRUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y python3 python3-pip\n\n# Optional: set a working directory\nWORKDIR /app\n\n# Copy your source code into the image\nCOPY src/ /app\n\n# Install any Python dependencies\n# RUN pip install -r requirements.txt   # uncomment if you have a requirements file\n\n# Command to run when the container starts\nCMD ["python3", "main.py"]   # replace main.py with your entry point\n```\n\nWith the Dockerfile correctly named and in the right location, the build\ncommand will succeed:\n\n```bash\n$ docker build -t myapp .\nSending build context to Docker daemon  2.048kB\n...\nSuccessfully built <image-id>\nSuccessfully tagged myapp:latest\n```\n\nNow you can run the container:\n\n```bash\ndocker run -it myapp\n```\n\nThat resolves the “no such file or directory: dockerfile” and “invalid reference\nformat” errors.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'gpt-oss:20b', 'created_at': '2025-10-17T10:52:51.145181096Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 277110934199, 'load_duration': 162687587, 'prompt_eval_count': 2334, 'prompt_eval_duration': 1739728195, 'eval_count': 24031, 'eval_duration': 275205981779, 'model_name': 'gpt-oss:20b'} id='run--f9c487df-82e0-4086-a15e-fda60fed6bba-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2334, 'output_tokens': 24031, 'total_tokens': 26365}
